From: Yong Liu <lyrids@me.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: fix peer use-after-free in HTT TX completion

ath11k_dp_tx_htt_tx_complete_buf() looks up the peer under
ab->base_lock but drops the lock before reading peer->sta.
ath11k_peer_unmap_event() can free the peer under the same lock in
between, so peer->sta is read from freed memory.

Read peer->sta while base_lock is still held, matching
ath11k_dp_tx_complete_msdu().

Signed-off-by: Yong Liu <lyrids@me.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -377,9 +377,10 @@
 		ieee80211_free_txskb(ar->hw, msdu);
 		return;
 	}
-	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 
 	status.sta = peer->sta;
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
+
 	status.info = info;
 	status.skb = msdu;
 
